= Staal's Backup Plan

Staal was never a true believer in converting his cabinet into a parliamentary one, and he undercut his own threat to call new elections by suggesting that no one would object if they were delayed beyond the constitutionally mandated 60 days. In reality, nothing could be further from the truth.

Even so, Staal now seeks to secure a decree—similar to the one he once offered Goodryke but which was never enacted, as the Assembly president simply ignored him. Should DuFour refuse to issue such a decree, it won’t signal a renewed commitment to constitutional norms. Rather, it would confirm the scope of the conspiracy against Staal—one that now includes the President himself.

- @root: [? if not staal_marcher_adopted: The <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> will strongly oppose any effort to violate the constitution. ?][? if staal_marcher_adopted: The nation needs a break from more polarizing elections. Let the chancellor govern. ?]